From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mm: lru_marie: read the per-memcg counter when reparenting
 MGLRU

lru_marie makes mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size() report Marie's node-global
NR_ZONE_LRU_BASE total for evictable LRUs, while mz->lru_zone_size keeps
only the memcg's legacy/orphan folios. lru_gen_reparent_memcg() pairs the
two:

	size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
	mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(parent_lruvec, lru, zid, size);
	mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid, -(long)size);

so every exiting cgroup credits its parent with the whole node LRU and
underflows its own counter:

  mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(...): lru_size -3105
  WARNING: mm/memcontrol.c at mem_cgroup_update_lru_size

lru_marie 1.0.0-rc1 fixed the same pairing in lruvec_reparent_lru()
(mm/swap.c) by reading mz->lru_zone_size directly. Do the same here.
Identical to the accessor when Marie is off.
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -4620,12 +4620,14 @@
 void lru_gen_reparent_memcg(struct mem_cgroup *memcg, struct mem_cgroup *parent, int nid)
 {
 	struct lruvec *child_lruvec, *parent_lruvec;
+	struct mem_cgroup_per_node *mz;
 	int type, zid;
 	struct zone *zone;
 	enum lru_list lru;
 
 	child_lruvec = get_lruvec(memcg, nid);
 	parent_lruvec = get_lruvec(parent, nid);
+	mz = container_of(child_lruvec, struct mem_cgroup_per_node, lruvec);
 
 	for_each_managed_zone_pgdat(zone, NODE_DATA(nid), zid, MAX_NR_ZONES - 1)
 		for (type = 0; type < ANON_AND_FILE; type++)
@@ -4633,7 +4635,14 @@
 
 	for_each_lru(lru) {
 		for_each_managed_zone_pgdat(zone, NODE_DATA(nid), zid, MAX_NR_ZONES - 1) {
-			unsigned long size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
+			/*
+			 * Read the child's own counter, not
+			 * mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(): lru_marie overrides that
+			 * accessor to report the node-global size for evictable
+			 * LRUs, so moving it here would credit the parent with the
+			 * whole node and underflow the child.
+			 */
+			unsigned long size = READ_ONCE(mz->lru_zone_size[zid][lru]);
 
 			if (!size)
 				continue;
